  </problem></exercise>
</example>
<exercise data-wait-for-event="RFM1">
  <problem>
    <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
    <para>Jada has a second option to earn money. She could help some neighbors with errands and computer work for $11 an hour. After reconsidering her schedule, Jada realizes that she has about 9 hours available to work one day of the weekend.</para>
    <para>Which option should she choose, sorting books at the bookstore or helping her neighbors? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Write your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>You could argue either way, depending on the assumptions you make.</para>
    <para>Jada should work at the bookstore because she would earn more there. Her pay would be $109.80, and after subtracting $7.15 for the bus fare, she would still earn $102.65. She would earn $99 from the other option.</para>
    <para>Jada should help her neighbors. Working 9 hours at the bookstore would mean a few dollars more than working 9 hours helping her neighbors, but it would also mean losing some personal time because of the travel involved.</para>
  </solution></exercise></section>
